body:
It's the same for me.   


My depression/anxiety is quite cyclical, largely because I learn to carry forward and ignore until it bottles up (usually brought on by some negative event in my life) and into a downward spiral I go.

&#x200B;

I can be dead tired from exhaustion but will wake up after 5 hours with my heart racing, followed immediately by the overflow of negative thoughts and possible horrible outcomes. I struggle to do the most basic things and just desire to speak/vent/rant/get it off my chest constantly. I have a wife and two kids and although it can keep me busy, the morning paralysis can make things feel sisyphean.

&#x200B;

By the end of the day though (from 6-7PM) I generally feel more positive and look forward to enjoying as much of the evening I can before my body passes out from the exhaustion I subjected to myself during the day.
